---
import ServiceSection from "../components/ServiceSection.astro";
import Endpoint from "../components/Endpoint.astro";
import RustSchema from "../components/RustSchema.astro";
---

<ServiceSection id="service-presence">
  <Fragment slot="title"><code>Pres</code> — presence</Fragment>
<p>Presence first defines a dynamic field table. Later updates contain field handles
    and a data blob. The table defines the values in the data blob.</p>
    <p class="endpoint-index">
      <a href="#presence-field-specs">Pres/1 FieldSpecAnnounce</a><a href="#presence-update-request">Pres/0 UpdateRequest</a><a href="#presence-update">Pres/0 UpdateNotify</a>
      <a href="#presence-statistics-subscribe">Pres/2 StatisticsSubscribe</a><a href="#presence-statistics-update">Pres/3 StatisticsUpdate</a>
      <a href="#presence-temporary">Pres/4 TemporaryPresence</a>
    </p>

    <Endpoint id="presence-field-specs" direction="server → client" phase="protected bootstrap" structure="generated order" status="verified">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Pres/1</code> Presence::FieldSpecAnnounce</Fragment>
      <p>Defines the numeric handles and storage rules used by subsequent presence
      updates.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`struct FieldSpecAnnounce {
    definitions: Vec<FieldSpec>, // count: 7 wire bits, 0..=100 accepted
}

struct FieldSpec {
    client_only: bool,
    writable: bool,
    ephemeral: bool,
    size: FieldSize,
    server_only: bool,
    identifier: u8,
    handle: u32,
}

enum FieldSize { Fixed(u16), Variable }`} />
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="presence-update-request" direction="client → server" phase="protected" structure="generated order" status="capture decoded">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Pres/0</code> Presence::UpdateRequest</Fragment>
      <p>Writes one typed presence value to a field handle for a presence record.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`struct UpdateRequest {
    value: PresenceValue, // selector: 5 wire bits
    handle: u32,
    generated_checksum: Bits<9>,
    presence_id: u32,
}`} />
      <p class="endpoint-note">The value choice covers integers, booleans, FourCC,
      strings, image entries, toon names and handles, profile addresses, account
      IDs, achievement values, and matchmaker handles. The selected arm determines
      its exact width before the field handle.</p>
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="presence-update" direction="server → client" phase="protected" structure="generated order" status="verified">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Pres/0</code> Presence::UpdateNotify</Fragment>
      <p>Updates online state and announced fields. Read field data in handle order.
      Use the fixed size from Pres/1 or the next variable size. A cleared handle
      removes its stored value. Local and master presence IDs identify the same
      stored record.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`struct UpdateNotify {
    _reserved_0: Reserved<19>,
    online: bool,
    local_presence_id: u32,
    master_presence_id: u32,
    field_data: Vec<u8>,       // byte count: 11 wire bits, 0..=1024; byte-aligned
    _reserved_1: Reserved<11>,
    cleared_handles: Vec<u32>, // count: 4 wire bits
    handles: Vec<u32>,         // count: 4 wire bits
    variable_sizes: Vec<u16>,  // count: 4 wire bits
    level_zero: Option<LevelZero>,
    server_only: u8,
}

struct LevelZero {
    is_last_packet: bool,
    target: u32,
}`} />
      <p class="endpoint-note"><code>FIELD_AVATAR</code> (<code>65555</code>) is
      a four-byte <code>ImageTableEntry</code>. Public channel membership usually
      supplies <code>FIELD_TOON_PROFILE</code> (<code>65556</code>); its
      12-byte profile address is followed through <code>Prfl/0</code> path
      <code>04</code> to obtain the selected avatar.</p>
      <p>The client reads all supported handles. Use the announced fixed size or the
      next variable size for each slice. Parse each slice by handle ID. All
      multi-byte values are big-endian.</p>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Handle</th><th>Field</th><th>Parse</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>0x50004</code></td><td>clan tag</td><td>byte0 = pair count, byte1 = trailing (0|1); byteCount = pairs&times;2 + trailing; remaining bytes UTF-8</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>0x00010005</code></td><td>account id</td><td>first four bytes <code>u32</code> (nonzero); the whisper-target account, priority 1</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>0x0001001b</code></td><td>social account id</td><td>first four bytes <code>u32</code>; account fallback, priority 2</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>65561</code></td><td>toon handle</td><td>region <code>u8</code>, program <code>u32</code>, realm <code>u32</code>, id <code>u64</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>65556</code></td><td>toon profile</td><td>label <code>u32</code>, id <code>u64</code> (a profile address)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>65555</code></td><td>avatar</td><td>tableId <code>u16</code>, offset <code>u16</code> (<code>ImageTableEntry</code>)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>0x50002</code></td><td>in game</td><td>single byte, true when <code>0x01</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>0x10020</code> / <code>0x10010</code></td><td>away</td><td>boolean; standing status</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>0x10022</code> / <code>0x10011</code></td><td>busy</td><td>boolean; standing status</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>0x00010003</code> / <code>0x00010009</code></td><td>session marks</td><td>set on entry, cleared on exit; presence is held while either is present, and drives leave detection</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="endpoint-note">Use this standing-state precedence: offline, in-game,
      busy or away, and available. For busy and away, the last write has precedence.
      The account-ID fields supply the target for an outbound whisper.</p>
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="presence-statistics-subscribe" direction="client → server" phase="protected" structure="generated order" status="live verified">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Pres/2</code> Presence::StatisticsSubscribe</Fragment>
      <p>Subscribes to or unsubscribes from the statistics stream. Temporary whisper
      targets use <code>Pres/4</code>.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`struct StatisticsSubscribe {
    on: bool,
}`} />
      <p class="endpoint-note">The logical record is 12 bits. Final padding makes
      the encoded record two bytes: <code>42 0c</code> when <code>on = 1</code>.</p>
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="presence-statistics-update" direction="server → client" phase="protected" structure="reflected order" status="capture observed">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Pres/3</code> Presence::StatisticsUpdate</Fragment>
      <p>Contains a server statistics update. Decode this record with the embedded
      metadata type. The client must map this route.</p>
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="presence-temporary" direction="bidirectional" phase="protected" structure="verified reflected order" status="verified">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>Pres/4</code> Presence::TemporaryPresence</Fragment>
      <p>Requests a connection-local presence ID for one or more target toons. This
      ID permits a whisper to an unknown toon. The immediate response supplies a
      result, and a later <code>Pres/0</code> update supplies the ID.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`// client → server
struct TemporaryPresenceRequest {
    toon_list: Vec<ToonHandle>, // count: 1..=10
}

struct ToonHandle {
    region: u8,
    program_id: FourCC,
    realm: u32,
    id: u64,
}

// server → client
struct TemporaryPresenceResponse {
    result: u16,
}`} />
      <p class="endpoint-note">Encode the program ID as a FourCC.</p>
    </Endpoint>
</ServiceSection>
